  "interpretation": [
    "The four day/night and clear/rain visual-condition combinations now each have five matched repetitions on this single integrated-GPU system.",
    "Frame-time tails vary between runs and remain worse than the 16.7 ms 60 Hz frame budget in several runs; per-condition medians and ranges are retained instead of claiming a stable 60 FPS result.",
    "Host CPU load and available memory vary across runs. The benchmark validates visibility, measured-window coverage and host telemetry, but these short runs do not establish thermal stability or a single root bottleneck.",
    "The fixture is synthetic and the path is a short fixed route. Cold/warm startup comparisons, real-city load, cross-cell walking/driving, mobile hardware and a 15-minute thermal run remain open.",
    "Keep Rust/Wasm/SIMD deferred until profiling of dense real-city traces proves a CPU-heavy kernel dominates a meaningful share of total latency. Improve visual quality only through locked-quality A/Bs with equal content and performance budgets."
  ],
